# Build-context exclusions for the REST image.
#
# This is a SECURITY control, not just a size optimization. The Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, and the Web SDK publishes `**/*.json` by default — so without the
# appsettings.Development.json line below, the local dev DB password and JWT
# secret end up inside the image that gets pushed to the public Docker Hub repo.
#
# bin/ and obj/ are produced on the Windows host; their project.assets.json
# carries Windows NuGet paths and would poison the in-container restore.

**/bin/
**/obj/

# Never ship local dev secrets (DB password, JWT secret, owner password hash).
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.json.user
.env

# Locally uploaded files — the deployed container gets its own named volume.
uploads/

# IDE / VCS noise
.vs/
*.user
Properties/launchSettings.json
